WEBVTT

00:00:09.535 --> 00:00:32.000
Black Cat presents Peter Pan by James Matthew Barrie. Adapted by Gina D. B. Clemen. Copyright Black Cat Publishing.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:38.200
Chapter 1 The Darling Family 

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:46.800
Wendy, John and Michael Darling live in a big house in London.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:53.424
It is a lovely house with a lot of rooms and a garden outside.

00:00:53.484 --> 00:00:58.296
They live with their parents, Mr. and Mrs. Darling.

00:00:58.356 --> 00:01:01.928
The darlings are a happy family.

00:01:01.988 --> 00:01:07.084
Mr. and Mrs. Darling love their children very much.

00:01:07.144 --> 00:01:12.618
Wendy is the first child and she is pretty.

00:01:12.678 --> 00:01:17.540
She has got long blonde hair and blue eyes.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:22.602
John is the second child and he is tall and thin.

00:01:22.662 --> 00:01:28.654
He has got brown hair and brown eyes and he wears glasses.

00:01:28.714 --> 00:01:36.401
Michael is the third child and he has got brown hair and blue eyes.

00:01:36.461 --> 00:01:41.028
The three children are very friendly.

00:01:41.088 --> 00:01:46.011
Wendy, John and Michael like playing in the nursery.

00:01:46.071 --> 00:01:51.344
It is a big sunny nursery and there are pictures on the walls.

00:01:51.404 --> 00:01:55.217
There are a lot of toys in the nursery.

00:01:55.277 --> 00:01:59.280
The children have a nanny called Nana.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:02.867
She is a big Newfoundland dog.

00:02:02.927 --> 00:02:07.876
She is a wonderful nanny and looks after the children.

00:02:07.936 --> 00:02:12.500
She loves them and they love her.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:16.513
Her kennel is in the nursery.

00:02:16.573 --> 00:02:23.960
One evening, Mr. and Mrs. Darling put on some very nice clothes.

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:28.234
They are going to a dinner party with their friends.

00:02:28.294 --> 00:02:31.690
Mrs. Darling goes to the nursery.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:34.876
The children are playing happily.

00:02:34.936 --> 00:02:41.008
Wendy sees her mother and says, What a lovely dress.

00:02:41.068 --> 00:02:44.550
Yes. Says John.
 
00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:52.074
You're wearing a beautiful dress. Thank you. Says Mrs Darling.
 
00:02:52.134 --> 00:02:56.676
Your father and I are going to a dinner party this evening.

00:02:56.736 --> 00:03:03.318
Then she looks at Nana and says, Nana, it's almost half past eight.

00:03:03.378 --> 00:03:06.770
It's time to put the children to bed.

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:15.006
Nana looks at Mrs Darling with her big brown eyes and barks.

00:03:15.066 --> 00:03:21.270
She goes to the bathroom and turns on the hot water for Michael's bath.

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:25.024
But Michael does not like having baths.

00:03:25.084 --> 00:03:28.775
No. Says little Michael.
 
00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:34.465
I don't want to have a bath! And I don't want to go to bed!.

00:03:34.524 --> 00:03:40.176
Nana is a good nanny and the children must listen to her.

00:03:40.236 --> 00:03:42.727
Michael has his bath.

00:03:42.787 --> 00:03:48.469
Then she gives the children their pajamas and they are ready for bed now.

00:03:48.529 --> 00:03:53.400
Mrs Darling comes to the nursery again and smiles.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.841
Good work, Nana.

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:59.133
The children are ready for bed.

00:03:59.193 --> 00:04:03.256
Nana looks at Mrs Darling and barks.

00:04:03.316 --> 00:04:07.078
Then she goes and sits near her kennel.

00:04:07.138 --> 00:04:12.280
I can hear a noise outside the window, says Wendy.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:14.750
Yes, says John.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:17.342
I can hear it too.

00:04:17.402 --> 00:04:23.485
Mrs Darling goes to the nursery window and is very surprised.

00:04:23.545 --> 00:04:28.840
She sees a young boy outside the nursery window.

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:33.934
Nana barks loudly and shuts the window quickly.

00:04:33.994 --> 00:04:40.576
The boy's shadow falls on the floor, and the young boy flies away.

00:04:40.636 --> 00:04:45.197
Who's there? asks Mrs Darling.
 
00:04:45.257 --> 00:04:51.579
She opens the window and looks outside, but she can't see anything.

00:04:51.639 --> 00:04:54.010
How strange.

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:56.224
There's no one here.

00:04:56.284 --> 00:05:01.920
She turns around and sees the boy's shadow on the floor.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:06.102
Wendy, John and Michael see it too.

00:05:06.162 --> 00:05:08.782
What's that?

00:05:08.842 --> 00:05:12.894
They ask, looking at the shadow on the floor.

00:05:12.953 --> 00:05:17.705
It's the poor boy's shadow. Says Mrs. Darling.
 
00:05:17.765 --> 00:05:21.677
What can we do with it? Asks Wendy.
 
00:05:21.736 --> 00:05:24.218
Let's put it in the drawer.

00:05:24.278 --> 00:05:26.192
Says Mrs. Darling.

00:05:26.252 --> 00:05:28.617
The children get into bed.

00:05:28.677 --> 00:05:31.738
Mr. Darling takes Nana to the garden.

00:05:31.798 --> 00:05:36.530
Then he goes to the sitting room and waits for Mrs. Darling.

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:43.023
Mrs. Darling sings to Wendy, John and Michael and kisses them.

00:05:43.083 --> 00:05:46.644
She is a wonderful mother.

00:05:46.704 --> 00:05:50.867
Soon the three children are sleeping.

00:05:50.926 --> 00:05:54.712
Mr. and Mrs. Darling go to their bedroom.

00:05:54.772 --> 00:06:00.397
They put on their coats and go to the dinner party.

00:06:00.457 --> 00:06:10.011
London The story you are reading starts in London in the early 1900s.

00:06:10.071 --> 00:06:15.994
London is a wonderful city and it is the capital of the United Kingdom.

00:06:16.054 --> 00:06:21.346
Today, almost 8 million people live there.

00:06:21.405 --> 00:06:25.180
London is a very green city.

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:28.466
There are more than 300 parks.

00:06:28.525 --> 00:06:35.150
Hyde Park is a very big park with more than 4,000 trees.

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:41.696
You can go biking in the park or you can ride a boat on the Serpentine Lake.

00:06:41.756 --> 00:06:46.210
In the summer, there are music concerts in the park.

00:06:46.270 --> 00:06:54.270
In Kensington Gardens, there is a statue of Peter Pan and a lot of visitors go and see it.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:59.978
The river Thames runs through the city and a lot of bridges cross it.

00:07:00.037 --> 00:07:05.932
You can take a lovely boat ride on the river Thames and ride under Tower Bridge.

00:07:05.992 --> 00:07:12.338
Big Ben is the name of an enormous clock on top of a tall tower.

00:07:12.398 --> 00:07:19.600
You can see the tower and the clock next to the Houses of Parliament on the river Thames.

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:23.686
The Tower of London is a very old tower.

00:07:23.746 --> 00:07:28.518
It was built between 1070 and 1100.

00:07:28.578 --> 00:07:33.720
You can visit the tower and see the Queen's crown jewels.

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:39.573
There are always a lot of interesting things to do and see in London.

00:07:39.633 --> 00:07:45.726
There are more than 240 important museums and many of them are free.

00:07:45.786 --> 00:07:50.690
There are also a lot of important theatres.

00:07:50.750 --> 00:08:00.932
Chapter 2. Peter's Shadow Everything is dark and silent in the nursery.

00:08:00.992 --> 00:08:06.448
Wendy, John and Michael are sleeping and dreaming.

00:08:06.508 --> 00:08:11.830
Outside the nursery window, there is a small ball of light.

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:14.629
The nursery window is open.

00:08:14.688 --> 00:08:23.630
Suddenly, the small ball of light comes into the nursery through the window and flies around.

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:28.262
It is a fairy called Tinker Bell.

00:08:28.322 --> 00:08:35.100
She is very small and lovely.

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:40.048
She is looking for something inside the nursery.

00:08:40.109 --> 00:08:48.396
After a moment, a young boy comes into the nursery through the open window and looks around.

00:08:48.456 --> 00:08:52.757
Tink? He says, Where are you?
 
00:08:52.817 --> 00:08:55.108
Where's my shadow?

00:08:55.168 --> 00:08:57.358
Please find it.

00:08:57.418 --> 00:09:03.250
Tinker Bell flies around the nursery and stops near a drawer.

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:08.123
She opens it carefully and finds his shadow.

00:09:08.182 --> 00:09:10.708
Then she gives it to him.

00:09:10.768 --> 00:09:15.395
Thank you, Tink," says the boy happily.

00:09:15.455 --> 00:09:18.987
He goes to the bathroom and gets some soap.

00:09:19.047 --> 00:09:24.230
Now I can put the shadow on my feet with some soap.

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:28.902
He tries to stick it on his feet, but he can't.

00:09:28.962 --> 00:09:33.114
Why can't I put my shadow on my feet?

00:09:33.174 --> 00:09:34.706
He thinks.

00:09:34.766 --> 00:09:38.480
Now I haven't got a shadow.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:43.054
He is very sad and starts to cry.

00:09:43.114 --> 00:09:48.207
Wendy hears the boy crying and she wakes up.

00:09:48.267 --> 00:09:52.839
She sees a young boy, but she is not afraid.

00:09:52.899 --> 00:09:57.081
He has got red hair and a friendly face.

00:09:57.141 --> 00:10:02.104
His clothes are made of green leaves, she thinks.

00:10:02.164 --> 00:10:06.387
What's this boy doing in the nursery?

00:10:06.447 --> 00:10:10.502
Little boy, why are you crying?

00:10:10.562 --> 00:10:12.142
Wendy asks.

00:10:12.202 --> 00:10:16.945
The boy smiles and asks, what's your name?

00:10:17.006 --> 00:10:22.420
My name's Wendy Moira Angela Darling.

00:10:22.460 --> 00:10:24.231
And what's yours?

00:10:24.291 --> 00:10:25.822
Peter Pan.

00:10:25.882 --> 00:10:29.734
Is that all? asks Wendy looking at him.
  
00:10:29.794 --> 00:10:33.456
Yes, that's all. Says Peter.
 
00:10:33.516 --> 00:10:38.738
Then he thinks, My name is very short.

00:10:38.798 --> 00:10:45.294
Wendy looks at his shadow on the floor and says, Is this your shadow?

00:10:45.354 --> 00:10:47.656
Yes. Says Peter.
 
00:10:47.716 --> 00:10:49.848
But I can't put it on.

00:10:49.908 --> 00:10:54.500
Wendy smiles and says, I can sew it on.

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:56.614
Can you?

00:10:56.674 --> 00:11:01.233
Oh please do it. Says Peter happily.
 
00:11:01.294 --> 00:11:07.744
Wendy gets her big sewing basket and sews on Peter's shadow carefully.

00:11:07.804 --> 00:11:11.526
Peter looks at her and he's very glad.

00:11:11.586 --> 00:11:16.500
After a few minutes Wendy says, I finished.

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:19.892
Now you've got your shadow again.

00:11:19.952 --> 00:11:24.296
Peter looks at the floor and he can see his shadow.

00:11:24.356 --> 00:11:28.300
He is happy and he dances around the nursery.

00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:33.126
Thank you, Wendy. He says.
 
00:11:33.186 --> 00:11:35.728
You're a wonderful girl.

00:11:35.788 --> 00:11:39.550
Do you really think so? asks Wendy.
 
00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:43.952
Yes, I do, says Peter, looking at Wendy.

00:11:44.012 --> 00:11:48.574
Wendy smiles and gives Peter a kiss on the cheek.

00:11:48.634 --> 00:11:51.256
Oh, says Peter.

00:11:51.315 --> 00:11:53.206
That's nice.

00:11:53.267 --> 00:11:57.678
How old are you, Peter? asks Wendy.
 
00:11:57.738 --> 00:12:00.300
Peter thinks for a moment and says, 

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:05.624
I don't know, but I'm young and I don't want to grow up.

00:12:05.684 --> 00:12:09.007
I don't want to become an adult.

00:12:09.068 --> 00:12:14.652
I want to be a boy forever and have lots of fun.

00:12:14.712 --> 00:12:19.206
Wendy listens to Peter and is surprised.

00:12:19.266 --> 00:12:22.492
Then Peter looks for his fairy.

00:12:22.552 --> 00:12:26.836
Suddenly he hears a noise and looks in a drawer.

00:12:26.896 --> 00:12:29.467
Little Tinker Bell flies out.

00:12:29.527 --> 00:12:32.318
Wendy is happy to see a fairy.

00:12:32.378 --> 00:12:34.618
But Tinker Bell is afraid.

00:12:34.678 --> 00:12:37.589
She hides behind the big clock.

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:41.601
Where do you live, Peter? asks Wendy.
 
00:12:41.661 --> 00:12:45.372
I sometimes live in Kensington Gardens.

00:12:45.432 --> 00:12:46.942
Says Peter.

00:12:47.002 --> 00:12:52.362
But most of the time I live in Neverland with the Lost Boys.

00:12:52.422 --> 00:12:55.682
Wendy does not understand.

00:12:55.742 --> 00:12:57.852
Neverland?

00:12:57.912 --> 00:13:00.513
The Lost Boys?

00:13:00.573 --> 00:13:02.300
Who are they?

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:08.285
The Lost Boys haven't got a mother or father, says Peter.

00:13:08.345 --> 00:13:12.616
They're alone in the world, and they live in Neverland.

00:13:12.676 --> 00:13:14.500
I'm their captain.

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:20.696
Neverland sounds like a wonderful place. says Wendy.
 
00:13:20.756 --> 00:13:23.198
It is, says Peter.

00:13:23.258 --> 00:13:25.930
And we have lots of fun there.

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:29.512
In Neverland, we fight the pirates.

00:13:29.572 --> 00:13:34.226
We swim in the lagoon with beautiful mermaids.

00:13:34.286 --> 00:13:39.009
A lot of lovely fairies live in the trees in the forest.

00:13:39.069 --> 00:13:43.524
They're my friends. What fun. Says Wendy.
 
00:13:43.584 --> 00:13:48.340
Well, I must go back to Neverland now, says Peter.

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:51.381
I must tell the Lost Boys a story.

00:13:51.441 --> 00:13:54.352
You know, they love stories.

00:13:54.412 --> 00:13:58.745
I know a lot of stories, says Wendy.

00:13:58.805 --> 00:14:02.629
Then come with me to Neverland, says Peter.

00:14:02.689 --> 00:14:05.492
You can tell us lots of stories.

00:14:05.552 --> 00:14:09.854
And you can see the beautiful mermaids in the lagoon.

00:14:09.914 --> 00:14:11.604
Come with me.

00:14:11.664 --> 00:14:13.616
We all want a mother.

00:14:13.776 --> 00:14:17.697
Oh, I can't come with you. Says Wendy.
 
00:14:17.757 --> 00:14:19.600
I can't fly.

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:23.040
I can teach you to fly. Says Peter.
 
00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:25.230
It's very easy.

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:29.672
Can you teach John and Michael to fly too?

00:14:29.732 --> 00:14:30.953
asks Wendy.

00:14:31.013 --> 00:14:33.554
Of course, says Peter.

00:14:33.614 --> 00:14:37.106
Wendy goes to John and Michael and says...

00:14:37.166 --> 00:14:39.828
Wake up. Quickly.
 
00:14:39.888 --> 00:14:41.970
Peter Pan is here.

00:14:42.030 --> 00:14:44.411
He's from Neverland.

00:14:44.471 --> 00:14:46.652
It's a fun place.

00:14:46.712 --> 00:14:49.084
John and Michael wake up.

00:14:49.144 --> 00:14:51.655
And they are very surprised.

00:14:51.715 --> 00:14:54.846
We can go to Neverland with him.

00:14:54.906 --> 00:14:56.257
says Wendy.

00:14:56.317 --> 00:14:58.958
But we must learn to fly.

00:14:59.018 --> 00:15:02.311
That's difficult. Says John.
  
00:15:02.371 --> 00:15:05.000
No, it's not. Says Peter.
 
00:15:05.060 --> 00:15:06.854
Look at me.

00:15:06.914 --> 00:15:11.958
Peter flies around the nursery and the children look at him.

00:15:12.018 --> 00:15:15.310
They are excited and try to fly.

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:19.234
But they fall on the beds and on the floor.

00:15:19.294 --> 00:15:23.465
It's impossible. They say.
 
00:15:23.525 --> 00:15:26.996
You need some fairy dust.

00:15:27.056 --> 00:15:29.458
Says Peter laughing.

00:15:29.518 --> 00:15:32.720
He puts some fairy dust on their heads.

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:35.041
Now try again.

00:15:35.102 --> 00:15:38.684
Wendy, John and Michael can fly now.

00:15:38.744 --> 00:15:41.300
And they are very happy.

00:15:41.360 --> 00:15:47.500
Look, I can fly. Says Wendy.
 
00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:52.786
We can too. Say John and Michael.
  
00:15:52.846 --> 00:15:56.160
Now we can go to Neverland with Peter.

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:58.532
Says Wendy Happily.

00:15:58.592 --> 00:16:01.573
Tink. Says Peter.
 
00:16:01.633 --> 00:16:05.166
Show us the way to Neverland.

00:16:05.226 --> 00:16:10.448
They follow Tinker Bell and fly out of the nursery window.

00:16:10.508 --> 00:16:14.080
There are a lot of stars in the night sky.

00:16:14.140 --> 00:16:22.000
In the garden, Nana looks at the sky and barks loudly.

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:27.646
Mr. and Mrs. Darling return from the dinner party at 11 o'clock.

00:16:27.706 --> 00:16:29.997
They go to the nursery.

00:16:30.057 --> 00:16:32.428
But it is empty.

00:16:32.488 --> 00:16:36.250
Where are the children?

00:16:36.310 --> 00:16:41.000
Chapter 3. Neverland 

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:46.176
Wendy, John and Michael fly over London.

00:16:46.236 --> 00:16:50.266
They see the river Thames and Tower Bridge.

00:16:50.326 --> 00:16:53.555
There are hundreds of lights in the city.

00:16:53.616 --> 00:17:04.653
Then they fly over big cities, small towns, tall mountains, green forests and blue seas.

00:17:04.714 --> 00:17:09.388
At last, they see an island in the sea below them.

00:17:09.448 --> 00:17:13.260
It is a beautiful island.

00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:18.669
That's Neverland! says Peter, looking down at the island.
 
00:17:18.729 --> 00:17:22.744
It is a sunny day now, but it's windy.

00:17:22.804 --> 00:17:27.900
Neverland! Say the children happily.
 
00:17:28.096 --> 00:17:30.687
Look John. Says Wendy.
 
00:17:30.747 --> 00:17:32.700
There's the lagoon.

00:17:32.800 --> 00:17:36.909
And there's the big forest. Says Michael.
 
00:17:36.969 --> 00:17:40.512
The three children are excited.

00:17:40.572 --> 00:17:46.405
The Lost Boys live in the green forest in a secret underground home.

00:17:46.465 --> 00:17:57.238
There are six lost boys and their names are Curly, Nibs, Tootles, Slightly, and the Twins and the Twins.

00:17:57.298 --> 00:18:01.569
They are waiting for Peter in the underground home.

00:18:01.629 --> 00:18:06.054
Suddenly they hear the voices of the pirates.

00:18:06.114 --> 00:18:08.807
I thought... I'm certain there were five of them.

00:18:08.867 --> 00:18:12.078
You want your eyes examining boy? Pass me that rope.
 
00:18:12.138 --> 00:18:16.769
I can hear the pirates. Says Tootles.
 
00:18:16.829 --> 00:18:19.229
They're in the forest.

00:18:19.289 --> 00:18:24.460
I am afraid of them. Says Slightly.
 
00:18:24.520 --> 00:18:28.121
What can we do? Asks curly.
 
00:18:28.181 --> 00:18:32.302
I'm not afraid of the pirates. Says Nibs.
 
00:18:32.362 --> 00:18:35.309
He goes out of the underground home.

00:18:35.369 --> 00:18:39.638
He hides behind a big tree and looks around.

00:18:39.698 --> 00:18:42.689
He sees the terrible pirates.

00:18:42.749 --> 00:18:48.521
They are walking in the forest and they are big and strong.

00:18:48.582 --> 00:18:53.314
They live on a pirate ship called the Jolly Roger.

00:18:53.374 --> 00:18:57.200
The pirates' captain is James Hook.

00:18:57.300 --> 00:19:02.430
He is a very bad pirate.

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:09.878
He has got black eyes, black hair, and a big black beard.

00:19:09.938 --> 00:19:12.409
He hates Peter Pan.

00:19:12.469 --> 00:19:15.122
He has got only one hand.

00:19:15.182 --> 00:19:18.314
The other hand is a hook.

00:19:18.374 --> 00:19:24.358
In the past, Peter cut off Captain Hook's right arm during a fight.

00:19:24.418 --> 00:19:30.113
A crocodile ate the arm because crocodiles are always hungry.

00:19:30.173 --> 00:19:36.368
Now the crocodile follows Captain Hook everywhere, because he wants to eat him.

00:19:36.428 --> 00:19:41.202
The crocodile has an alarm clock in its stomach.

00:19:41.262 --> 00:19:45.625
Captain Hook can always hear it.

00:19:45.686 --> 00:19:54.052
We must find Peter Pan and the Lost Boys, says Captain Hook angrily.

00:19:54.113 --> 00:19:59.802
I know they live in this forest, but where?

00:19:59.862 --> 00:20:06.530
The pirates look everywhere, but they cannot find the secret underground home.

00:20:06.590 --> 00:20:10.832
Suddenly, Captain Hook hears the alarm clock.

00:20:10.892 --> 00:20:16.400
Tick, tock, tick, tock.

00:20:16.500 --> 00:20:20.514
The crocodile is near. cries Captain Hook.
 
00:20:20.575 --> 00:20:22.215
He wants to eat me.

00:20:22.275 --> 00:20:25.696
We must leave the forest quickly.

00:20:25.756 --> 00:20:29.950
He runs away, and the pirates follow him.

00:20:30.010 --> 00:20:34.556
Soon some American Indians come to the forest.

00:20:34.616 --> 00:20:39.438
They walk silently and carry bows and arrows.

00:20:39.498 --> 00:20:42.010
They are looking for the pirates.

00:20:42.070 --> 00:20:44.672
The pirates are their enemies.

00:20:44.732 --> 00:20:47.924
Their leader is Tiger Lily.

00:20:47.984 --> 00:20:52.798
She is the lovely daughter of the American Indian chief.

00:20:52.858 --> 00:20:55.449
She likes Peter Pan a lot.

00:20:55.509 --> 00:21:00.484
The Indians cannot find the pirates and they soon go away.

00:21:00.544 --> 00:21:06.390
Now the Lost Boys can leave the underground home and play in the forest.

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:12.964
Nibs looks at the sky and says, Look, there's a white bird in the sky.

00:21:13.024 --> 00:21:17.000
The Lost Boys look at the sky and Curly asks, 

00:21:17.100 --> 00:21:19.407
Is it really a bird?

00:21:19.467 --> 00:21:21.978
Of course it's a bird.

00:21:22.038 --> 00:21:23.730
Says Tinker Bell.

00:21:23.790 --> 00:21:26.261
It's a Wendy bird.

00:21:26.321 --> 00:21:28.488
You must shoot it.

00:21:28.548 --> 00:21:33.015
Sometimes Tinker Bell is a bad fairy.

00:21:33.075 --> 00:21:37.486
She knows that it is Wendy, but she doesn't like her.

00:21:37.546 --> 00:21:41.366
Nibs takes his bow and arrow and looks at the sky.

00:21:41.426 --> 00:21:45.347
He shoots Wendy, and she falls to the ground.

00:21:45.407 --> 00:21:48.748
Then the Lost Boys go and see Wendy.

00:21:48.808 --> 00:21:54.048
She's not a bird. They say.
 
00:21:54.108 --> 00:21:57.930
She's a lovely girl.

00:21:57.990 --> 00:22:04.812
Peter flies down with John and Michael and asks, Where's Wendy?

00:22:04.872 --> 00:22:08.572
Tootles says, Here she is.

00:22:08.632 --> 00:22:14.204
Peter goes to her and asks, Wendy, are you alright?

00:22:14.264 --> 00:22:18.795
Wendy slowly opens her eyes and smiles at Peter.

00:22:18.855 --> 00:22:22.400
Yes, I'm alright. She says, 

00:22:22.460 --> 00:22:27.703
I'm lucky because the arrow hit the button of my night dress.

00:22:27.764 --> 00:22:31.202
The Lost Boys are very sorry.

00:22:31.262 --> 00:22:34.804
Poor Wendy. Says Curly.
 
00:22:34.864 --> 00:22:37.274
What can we do?

00:22:37.335 --> 00:22:42.077
I've got a good idea. Says Slightly.
 
00:22:42.138 --> 00:22:46.080
We can build her a little house.

00:22:46.140 --> 00:22:51.072
When the little house is ready, the Lost Boys go and tell Wendy.

00:22:51.132 --> 00:22:56.710
Come and see the little house Wendy. Says Tootles.
 
00:22:56.770 --> 00:22:59.496
Do you like it?

00:22:59.556 --> 00:23:01.617
Ask the Lost Boys.

00:23:01.677 --> 00:23:05.850
Yes, I do. Says Wendy happily.
  
00:23:05.910 --> 00:23:08.372
It's a nice little house.

00:23:08.432 --> 00:23:09.823
Thank you.

00:23:09.883 --> 00:23:13.666
Wendy, can you be our mother now?

00:23:13.726 --> 00:23:15.338
Ask Nibs.

00:23:15.398 --> 00:23:20.762
Can you tell us bedtime stories before we go to bed?

00:23:20.822 --> 00:23:24.588
Yes, please. Says Tootles.
 
00:23:24.648 --> 00:23:27.734
Come and be our mother.

00:23:27.794 --> 00:23:30.704
Of course. Says Wendy.
 
00:23:30.764 --> 00:23:36.266
Come in and I can tell you the story of Cinderella.

00:23:36.326 --> 00:23:43.418
They listen to Wendy's story and like it a lot.

00:23:43.478 --> 00:23:47.849
Fairies and their magic.

00:23:47.909 --> 00:23:54.106
People all over the world have stories about fairies and their magic.

00:23:54.166 --> 00:23:59.974
Some of these stories are very old and some of them are called fairy tales.

00:24:00.034 --> 00:24:07.578
Fairies are part of British, Irish, Northern European and other cultures.

00:24:07.638 --> 00:24:12.640
In Peter Pan, Tinker Bell is Peter's fairy.

00:24:12.700 --> 00:24:17.520
Peter says that the fairies in Neverland are his good friends.

00:24:17.580 --> 00:24:23.098
In Pinocchio, there is a kind fairy called the Blue Fairy.

00:24:23.158 --> 00:24:25.670
She always helps Pinocchio.

00:24:25.730 --> 00:24:31.592
In Cinderella, a fairy godmother is Cinderella's good friend.

00:24:31.653 --> 00:24:36.095
There are fairies in one of William Shakespeare's plays too.

00:24:36.155 --> 00:24:43.780
In a Midsummer Night's Dream, Oberon and Titania are the king and queen of the fairies.

00:24:43.840 --> 00:24:49.124
They live in the forest and are important characters in the play.

00:24:49.184 --> 00:24:52.824
What some people say about fairies.

00:24:52.884 --> 00:24:55.986
They are small and have wings.

00:24:56.046 --> 00:25:01.807
They live in the forest, in trees, in flowers and in gardens.

00:25:01.867 --> 00:25:06.208
They are sometimes good and sometimes bad.

00:25:06.269 --> 00:25:07.829
They are magic.

00:25:07.889 --> 00:25:12.621
They can do good things and bad things.

00:25:12.681 --> 00:25:18.000
Chapter 4. Danger in the Lagoon 

00:25:18.500 --> 00:25:26.120
Peter, Wendy, John, Michael and the Lost Boys often go to the mermaid's lagoon.

00:25:26.180 --> 00:25:29.212
The water is blue and beautiful.

00:25:29.272 --> 00:25:33.254
They like swimming and playing in the blue lagoon.

00:25:33.314 --> 00:25:38.962
Beautiful mermaids live here and they are Peter's friends.

00:25:39.022 --> 00:25:43.100
They have got long hair and are very pretty.

00:25:43.160 --> 00:25:51.356
They play mermaid games and then sit on Marooners' Rock and comb their long hair.

00:25:51.416 --> 00:25:55.520
They sit in the sun and talk and laugh.

00:25:55.580 --> 00:25:59.300
The children like the mermaids and John says, 

00:25:59.400 --> 00:26:02.489
I want to catch a mermaid.

00:26:02.549 --> 00:26:08.090
He tries, but the mermaid jumps into the water and swims away.

00:26:08.150 --> 00:26:20.123
Everyone laughs. No. It's very difficult to catch a mermaid. Says Peter.
  
00:26:20.183 --> 00:26:23.700
Suddenly Peter hears a noise and says, 

00:26:23.760 --> 00:26:25.855
The pirates are coming.

00:26:25.915 --> 00:26:27.451
I can hear them.

00:26:27.511 --> 00:26:33.412
John, Michael and the Lost Boys jump into the water and swim away.

00:26:33.472 --> 00:26:35.793
They are afraid of the pirates.

00:26:35.853 --> 00:26:38.235
But Wendy stays with Peter.

00:26:38.295 --> 00:26:41.658
They hide behind Marooners' Rock.

00:26:41.718 --> 00:26:47.212
A small boat with two pirates is coming to the lagoon.

00:26:47.272 --> 00:26:49.644
One pirate is Smee.

00:26:49.704 --> 00:26:53.204
He is old and wears glasses.

00:26:53.264 --> 00:26:56.233
The other pirate is Starkey.

00:26:56.293 --> 00:26:59.884
He is young and has got a long nose.

00:26:59.944 --> 00:27:05.886
Tiger Lily is on the boat, and she is a prisoner of the pirates.

00:27:05.946 --> 00:27:09.097
Let's leave her on this rock.

00:27:09.157 --> 00:27:10.688
says Smee.

00:27:10.748 --> 00:27:15.769
When the sea rises, she's going to die.

00:27:15.830 --> 00:27:19.121
The two pirates laugh loudly.

00:27:19.181 --> 00:27:27.500
It is almost night, and it is dark.

00:27:27.600 --> 00:27:32.115
Poor Tiger Lily. thinks Peter.
 
00:27:32.175 --> 00:27:36.810
She is our good friend. I must save her.
 
00:27:36.870 --> 00:27:39.342
But what can I do?

00:27:39.403 --> 00:27:45.278
He thinks for a minute and then imitates Captain Hook's voice.

00:27:45.338 --> 00:27:50.400
Cut the ropes and let Tiger Lily go.

00:27:50.500 --> 00:27:52.834
Do as I say, Smee.

00:27:52.894 --> 00:27:55.176
Let her go."

00:27:55.236 --> 00:28:01.414
The two pirates hear Captain Hook's voice, and are very surprised.

00:28:01.474 --> 00:28:05.607
They look at each other, and then they look around.

00:28:05.668 --> 00:28:08.800
Starkey, says Smee.

00:28:08.860 --> 00:28:12.181
Can you hear Hook's voice?

00:28:12.241 --> 00:28:16.243
Yes, says Starkey, looking around.

00:28:16.303 --> 00:28:19.494
But I don't see Hook.

00:28:19.554 --> 00:28:23.866
We must listen to Hook and cut the ropes.

00:28:23.926 --> 00:28:25.416
says Smee.

00:28:25.476 --> 00:28:29.168
Are you sure? Asks Starkey.
 
00:28:29.228 --> 00:28:33.090
Of course I'm sure. says Smee.
 
00:28:33.150 --> 00:28:36.950
Starkey gets a knife and cuts the rope.

00:28:37.010 --> 00:28:39.160
Tiger Lily is free.

00:28:39.220 --> 00:28:43.381
She jumps into the water and swims away.

00:28:43.441 --> 00:28:51.192
Captain Hook is on his ship, the Jolly Roger, and he sees everything.

00:28:51.252 --> 00:28:56.033
He is very angry because Tiger Lily is free.

00:28:56.093 --> 00:29:02.724
Peter Pan is very clever, thinks Captain Hook.

00:29:02.784 --> 00:29:06.144
I must fight him.

00:29:06.204 --> 00:29:11.703
Captain Hook jumps into the water and swims to the rock.

00:29:11.763 --> 00:29:13.673
He fights with Peter.

00:29:13.733 --> 00:29:15.884
It is a long fight.

00:29:15.944 --> 00:29:19.884
Captain Hook hurts Peter with his big hook.

00:29:19.944 --> 00:29:22.825
But Peter does not stop fighting.

00:29:22.885 --> 00:29:24.626
He is brave.

00:29:24.686 --> 00:29:27.756
At last, Peter wins the fight.

00:29:27.816 --> 00:29:33.006
Captain Hook is angry and swims back to the Jolly Roger.

00:29:33.066 --> 00:29:37.799
Peter and Wendy are now alone on the rock.

00:29:37.859 --> 00:29:41.062
What a terrible fight, Peter!

00:29:41.122 --> 00:29:43.784
says Wendy, looking at Peter's hand.

00:29:43.844 --> 00:29:47.968
His hand is badly hurt after the fight with Captain Hook.

00:29:48.028 --> 00:29:50.357
Yes, says Peter.

00:29:50.418 --> 00:29:54.636
But I'm not afraid of hook or the pirates.

00:29:54.696 --> 00:29:59.508
You're a very brave boy, says Wendy, smiling.

00:29:59.568 --> 00:30:01.818
Look, says Peter.

00:30:01.878 --> 00:30:06.300
The sea is rising and we are in great danger here.

00:30:06.400 --> 00:30:10.202
What can we do? asks Wendy.
 
00:30:10.262 --> 00:30:16.244
We must leave this rock immediately, says Peter, looking at the sea.

00:30:16.304 --> 00:30:19.221
Oh, Peter, says Wendy.

00:30:19.282 --> 00:30:24.050
I can't swim or fly because I'm very tired.

00:30:24.110 --> 00:30:26.051
Peter thinks for a moment.

00:30:26.111 --> 00:30:29.562
He sees a big kite with a long tail.

00:30:29.622 --> 00:30:32.834
It is flying slowly over the lagoon.

00:30:32.894 --> 00:30:36.360
He quickly takes the tail of the kite and says, 

00:30:36.410 --> 00:30:42.708
Wendy, hold on to this tail and fly away with the kite.

00:30:42.768 --> 00:30:46.257
Wendy flies away with the kite.

00:30:46.317 --> 00:30:49.116
The sea is rising quickly.

00:30:49.176 --> 00:30:52.769
Peter thinks, I must fly away.

00:30:52.829 --> 00:30:59.414
When Peter gets home, everyone is happy to see him.

00:30:59.474 --> 00:31:04.400
Chapter 5. A Secret Place.

00:31:04.500 --> 00:31:11.342
The underground home is a secret place in the big forest.

00:31:11.402 --> 00:31:16.165
It is a safe place because no one knows where it is.

00:31:16.225 --> 00:31:20.456
There is only one big room with a fireplace.

00:31:20.516 --> 00:31:24.008
It is a happy, warm home.

00:31:24.068 --> 00:31:27.840
Wendy, John and Michael are very happy there.

00:31:27.900 --> 00:31:30.921
Wendy is a wonderful mother.

00:31:30.981 --> 00:31:34.512
She cooks and sews for everyone.

00:31:34.572 --> 00:31:40.144
Every evening, after dinner, everyone sits in front of the fireplace.

00:31:40.204 --> 00:31:43.618
Wendy tells great bedtime stories.

00:31:43.678 --> 00:31:51.012
The Lost Boys love these stories and are happy because they finally have a mother.

00:31:51.072 --> 00:31:56.643
John and Michael are happy because there is an exciting adventure every day.

00:31:56.703 --> 00:31:59.144
They are never bored.

00:31:59.204 --> 00:32:02.334
Peter Pan is the perfect father.

00:32:02.394 --> 00:32:06.645
He brings home food and protects his family.

00:32:06.705 --> 00:32:11.544
He and Wendy play games with the children and laugh with them.

00:32:11.604 --> 00:32:15.614
Everyone is having a wonderful time.

00:32:15.674 --> 00:32:21.986
But in London, Mr. and Mrs. Darling are not happy.

00:32:22.046 --> 00:32:27.807
They are very sad because they can't find their three children.

00:32:27.867 --> 00:32:30.908
And Nana is sad too.

00:32:30.968 --> 00:32:34.908
Where are our three children?

00:32:34.968 --> 00:32:37.039
They think.

00:32:37.099 --> 00:32:41.170
Wendy sometimes thinks about her parents.

00:32:41.231 --> 00:32:44.013
One evening, she says.

00:32:44.073 --> 00:32:50.088
This evening, I'm going to tell you a new bedtime story.

00:32:50.148 --> 00:32:53.411
It takes place in England.

00:32:53.471 --> 00:32:59.226
Everyone sits down in front of the fireplace and listens to her.

00:32:59.286 --> 00:33:04.050
In the city of London, there are two parents.

00:33:04.110 --> 00:33:10.066
They're very sad because they can't find their three children.

00:33:10.126 --> 00:33:15.120
Every night they leave the nursery window open.

00:33:15.180 --> 00:33:18.462
They want their children to return.

00:33:18.522 --> 00:33:24.835
They wait and wait, but their three children don't return.

00:33:24.895 --> 00:33:29.558
These poor parents are terribly sad.

00:33:29.618 --> 00:33:31.958
But when did he?

00:33:32.019 --> 00:33:34.150
Say John and Michael.

00:33:34.210 --> 00:33:38.046
That's the story of our parents.

00:33:38.106 --> 00:33:41.400
Peter listens to the story and says, 

00:33:41.500 --> 00:33:49.117
Sometimes parents forget their children and other children take their place.

00:33:49.178 --> 00:33:53.270
Wendy, John and Michael are surprised.

00:33:53.330 --> 00:33:55.342
They look at Peter.

00:33:55.402 --> 00:33:58.954
Are you sure, Peter? asks Wendy.
 
00:33:59.014 --> 00:34:02.362
Yes, I'm sure, says Peter.

00:34:02.423 --> 00:34:09.833
Perhaps there are other children in our nursery and in our beds, says Wendy.

00:34:09.894 --> 00:34:15.577
John, Michael, we must go home immediately.

00:34:15.637 --> 00:34:22.512
John and Michael look at Wendy and say, Do we really have to go?

00:34:22.573 --> 00:34:26.609
Yes, we must go home, says Wendy.

00:34:26.669 --> 00:34:30.055
Quickly, we haven't got much time.

00:34:30.115 --> 00:34:35.058
But we're happy here in Neverland with Peter and the Lost Boys.

00:34:35.118 --> 00:34:36.329
Says John.

00:34:36.390 --> 00:34:40.942
There's a new adventure every day. Says Michael.
 
00:34:41.002 --> 00:34:44.325
And we're never bored. Says John.
 
00:34:44.385 --> 00:34:50.309
Neverland is a wonderful place. Oh Wendy.
 
00:34:50.369 --> 00:34:52.700
Say the Lost Boys.

00:34:52.760 --> 00:34:56.070
Please don't go away.

00:34:56.130 --> 00:34:58.679
Don't leave us.

00:34:58.739 --> 00:35:05.224
Wendy looks at the Lost Boys and says, Please don't be sad.

00:35:05.284 --> 00:35:08.708
You can come to London and live with us.

00:35:08.768 --> 00:35:12.441
You can be part of the Darling family.

00:35:12.511 --> 00:35:17.436
Ah, Wendy. Say the Lost Boys.
  
00:35:17.496 --> 00:35:22.236
Thank you. That's wonderful.
 
00:35:22.296 --> 00:35:28.234
We can have a real family in London.

00:35:28.294 --> 00:35:33.606
Nibs and Tootles jump up and down and laugh.

00:35:33.666 --> 00:35:36.957
The other lost boys dance around the room.

00:35:37.017 --> 00:35:39.448
They are very happy.

00:35:39.508 --> 00:35:42.629
Peter is not happy.

00:35:42.689 --> 00:35:45.890
I'm not coming with you to London.

00:35:45.950 --> 00:35:49.491
Everyone is surprised and looks at him.

00:35:49.551 --> 00:35:52.508
Why? asks Wendy.
 
00:35:52.569 --> 00:35:56.898
I don't want to grow up, says Peter.

00:35:56.958 --> 00:36:00.429
I don't want to become an adult.

00:36:00.490 --> 00:36:03.412
I want to be a boy forever.

00:36:03.472 --> 00:36:06.513
But Peter, says Wendy.

00:36:06.573 --> 00:36:09.655
All boys and girls grow up.

00:36:09.715 --> 00:36:12.100
They become adults.

00:36:12.200 --> 00:36:15.788
No, says Peter angrily.

00:36:15.848 --> 00:36:18.550
I don't want to grow up.

00:36:18.610 --> 00:36:22.453
You can go, but I'm not coming.

00:36:22.514 --> 00:36:26.456
He turns around and looks at the wall.

00:36:26.516 --> 00:36:36.018
Wendy, John, Michael and the Lost Boys say goodbye to Peter and leave the underground home.

00:36:36.078 --> 00:36:44.719
They start to walk in the forest, but they don't know that the pirates are hiding behind the trees.

00:36:44.779 --> 00:36:46.919
They are waiting for them.

00:36:46.979 --> 00:36:50.500
Suddenly the pirates jump out of the forest, 

00:36:50.600 --> 00:36:55.474
The children are very surprised and try to run away.

00:36:55.534 --> 00:37:02.148
But there are a lot of pirates and they take the children to the Jolly Roger.

00:37:02.208 --> 00:37:08.420
Peter is inside the underground home and he does not hear anything.

00:37:08.480 --> 00:37:16.675
He sits in front of the fireplace and thinks about Wendy, John and Michael and the Lost Boys.

00:37:16.735 --> 00:37:21.134
He is sad without them.

00:37:21.194 --> 00:37:25.322
There is someone at the door.

00:37:25.382 --> 00:37:29.543
Peter goes to the door and asks, Who's there?

00:37:29.603 --> 00:37:34.500
He hears the sound of little bells.

00:37:34.600 --> 00:37:36.365
And opens the door.

00:37:36.425 --> 00:37:38.800
Tinker Bell flies in and says, 

00:37:38.900 --> 00:37:42.087
The children are with the pirates.

00:37:42.147 --> 00:37:45.908
What do you mean, Tink? asks Peter.
 
00:37:45.968 --> 00:37:55.049
Wendy, John, Michael and the Lost Boys are on the Jolly Roger with Captain Hook. says Tinker Bell.
 
00:37:55.109 --> 00:37:56.980
They're in danger!

00:37:57.040 --> 00:37:59.621
Oh no! says Peter.
 
00:37:59.681 --> 00:38:01.741
We must save them!

00:38:01.802 --> 00:38:04.900
Let's go to the Jolly Roger quickly!

00:38:05.000 --> 00:38:07.913
I want to fight Hook!

00:38:07.974 --> 00:38:15.466
Peter and Tinker Bell leave the underground home and fly to the Jolly Roger.

00:38:15.526 --> 00:38:20.000
The Great Ormond Street Hospital for Children

00:38:20.100 --> 00:38:27.140
In London there is a hospital for sick children called the Great Ormond Street Hospital for Children.

00:38:27.200 --> 00:38:30.844
J.M.Barry likes children very much.

00:38:30.904 --> 00:38:33.798
He wants children to be well and happy.

00:38:33.858 --> 00:38:38.670
He often visits this hospital because he wants to help the children.

00:38:38.730 --> 00:38:41.138
Barry is a kind man.

00:38:41.198 --> 00:38:51.346
In 1929, he decides that all the money from book sales, films and theatre plays of Peter Pan goes to the hospital.

00:38:51.406 --> 00:38:53.598
And this continues today.

00:38:53.658 --> 00:38:59.782
This money helps the hospital, the children, the doctors and the nurses.

00:38:59.842 --> 00:39:05.147
The children at the hospital can watch the play Peter Pan once a year.

00:39:05.207 --> 00:39:10.316
This is a very happy moment for them.

00:39:10.377 --> 00:39:15.300
Chapter 6. The Pirate Ship. 

00:39:15.400 --> 00:39:22.420
The Jolly Roger is a big pirate ship in the bay near Kidd's Creek.

00:39:22.480 --> 00:39:28.063
On the ship, there is a black flag with a white skull on it.

00:39:28.124 --> 00:39:30.915
It is the pirate's flag.

00:39:30.976 --> 00:39:37.500
It is night time, and there is a yellow moon in the dark sky.

00:39:37.560 --> 00:39:41.350
Peter sees the children on the pirate ship.

00:39:41.410 --> 00:39:46.738
They are prisoners of Captain Hook, and they are afraid of him.

00:39:46.798 --> 00:39:55.309
Captain Hook looks at the children and says, Peter Pan can't save you now.

00:39:55.369 --> 00:39:58.300
You're my prisoners.

00:39:58.360 --> 00:40:04.700
He starts to laugh, and the other pirates laugh too.

00:40:04.800 --> 00:40:09.452
Smee, come here, says Captain Hook.

00:40:09.512 --> 00:40:12.978
Yes, sir. says Smee.
 
00:40:13.038 --> 00:40:17.471
Get the plank, ready for these children.

00:40:17.531 --> 00:40:19.382
Says Captain Hook.

00:40:19.442 --> 00:40:22.974
You're all right, sir. says Smee.
 
00:40:23.034 --> 00:40:26.056
He goes to get the long plank.

00:40:26.116 --> 00:40:28.257
What's the plank?

00:40:28.317 --> 00:40:31.438
asks John, looking at Wendy.

00:40:31.498 --> 00:40:34.960
Ha! laughs Captain Hook.
 
00:40:35.020 --> 00:40:39.108
You don't know what the plank is.

00:40:39.168 --> 00:40:44.226
You must all walk the plank tonight.

00:40:44.286 --> 00:40:48.658
I don't understand," says John.

00:40:48.718 --> 00:40:57.623
First you walk the plank, and then you fall into the sea, says Captain Hook.

00:40:57.684 --> 00:41:02.166
And in the sea, there's a hungry crocodile.

00:41:02.226 --> 00:41:06.822
He wants to eat you.

00:41:06.882 --> 00:41:10.947
shout the children.

00:41:11.008 --> 00:41:12.998
They are afraid.

00:41:13.058 --> 00:41:21.811
But perhaps I can save two of you, says Captain Hook, looking at the children.

00:41:21.871 --> 00:41:25.382
I want two young pirates.

00:41:25.442 --> 00:41:28.913
Who wants to be a pirate?

00:41:28.973 --> 00:41:35.000
The Lost Boys look at John, and John looks at Michael and says, 

00:41:35.100 --> 00:41:38.336
I don't want to walk the plank.

00:41:38.396 --> 00:41:42.658
I don't want to be food for that hungry crocodile.
 
00:41:42.718 --> 00:41:46.699
What do you mean, John?" asks Michael.
 
00:41:46.759 --> 00:41:49.090
Well, says John.

00:41:49.150 --> 00:41:52.161
The life of a pirate is exciting.

00:41:52.221 --> 00:41:54.522
There are a lot of adventures.

00:41:54.582 --> 00:41:57.093
Let's be pirates, Michael.

00:41:57.153 --> 00:42:00.094
Michael does not know what to say.

00:42:00.154 --> 00:42:02.724
He and John look at Wendy.

00:42:02.784 --> 00:42:07.286
That's a terrible idea, John, says Wendy.

00:42:07.346 --> 00:42:09.938
I'm surprised at you.

00:42:09.998 --> 00:42:17.022
Captain Hook moves his hook in front of their faces and laughs loudly.

00:42:17.082 --> 00:42:23.066
I want an answer from you, says Captain Hook.

00:42:23.127 --> 00:42:26.128
Do you want to be pirates?

00:42:26.188 --> 00:42:29.760
Yes or no?

00:42:29.820 --> 00:42:36.774
John and Michael look at each other and then say, Never!

00:42:36.835 --> 00:42:41.458
What? says Captain Hook angrily.
 
00:42:41.518 --> 00:42:47.074
Then you must walk the plank and die.

00:42:47.134 --> 00:42:49.496
Wendy is afraid.

00:42:49.556 --> 00:42:52.998
She loves her brothers and the Lost Boys.

00:42:53.058 --> 00:42:55.433
She has tears in her eyes.

00:42:55.493 --> 00:43:01.438
A pirate shouts, who's the first to walk the plank?

00:43:01.498 --> 00:43:05.890
At that moment, everyone hears a loud noise.

00:43:05.950 --> 00:43:09.721
Tick, tock, tick, tock.

00:43:09.781 --> 00:43:15.474
Oh no. It's the crocodile, says Captain Hook.
 
00:43:15.534 --> 00:43:18.794
He wants to eat me.

00:43:18.855 --> 00:43:25.276
His face is white, and he runs to his cabin and hides there.

00:43:25.337 --> 00:43:31.538
The crocodile is hungry tonight," says a pirate.

00:43:31.598 --> 00:43:35.660
Someone must walk the plank.

00:43:35.720 --> 00:43:39.072
Who's the first to walk the plank?

00:43:39.132 --> 00:43:43.004
asks Smee, looking at John and Michael.

00:43:43.064 --> 00:43:45.054
Let's go!

00:43:45.114 --> 00:43:50.924
Suddenly, Peter Pan arrives, and Tinker Bell follows him.

00:43:50.984 --> 00:43:55.832
Wendy, John, Michael and the Lost Boys cheer happily.

00:43:55.892 --> 00:43:58.904
They are very happy to see him.

00:43:58.964 --> 00:44:01.626
Peter's here.

00:44:01.687 --> 00:44:03.197
They say.

00:44:03.257 --> 00:44:06.469
He's going to save us.

00:44:06.530 --> 00:44:12.222
Captain Hook comes out of his cabin and sees Peter Pan.

00:44:12.283 --> 00:44:16.161
He and his pirates are very angry.

00:44:16.221 --> 00:44:19.600
Hook takes his long sword and says, 

00:44:19.700 --> 00:44:24.402
I'm going to fight you, Peter Pan.

00:44:24.462 --> 00:44:32.276
This is your last fight, because tonight you're going to die.

00:44:32.336 --> 00:44:38.040
Hook fights with his long sword and with his big hook.

00:44:38.100 --> 00:44:43.204
Peter is very brave and fights with his small sword.

00:44:43.264 --> 00:44:48.554
He pushes Hook to the back of the ship, It is a terrible fight.

00:44:48.614 --> 00:44:53.425
John, Michael and the Lost Boys fight the pirates.

00:44:53.485 --> 00:44:59.577
After a long fight, they throw the pirates into the sea.

00:44:59.637 --> 00:45:04.678
Peter and Captain Hook fight all over the ship.

00:45:04.739 --> 00:45:07.469
Their swords make a lot of noise.

00:45:07.529 --> 00:45:11.670
Suddenly, Peter pushes Captain Hook into the sea.

00:45:11.730 --> 00:45:16.621
Hook shouts, oh no!

00:45:16.681 --> 00:45:23.054
He falls into the sea and into the mouth of the hungry crocodile.

00:45:23.114 --> 00:45:25.786
Everyone cheers.

00:45:25.846 --> 00:45:29.758
Oh, Peter. Says Wendy happily.
 
00:45:29.818 --> 00:45:32.950
You're a very brave boy.

00:45:33.010 --> 00:45:37.042
She smiles and kisses him on the cheek.

00:45:37.102 --> 00:45:43.396
Peter is happy and says, Now the Jolly Roger is ours.

00:45:43.456 --> 00:45:53.644
We can go home. Everyone shouts, Let's go!
 
00:45:53.704 --> 00:45:58.600
Chapter 7. Back in London. 

00:45:58.700 --> 00:46:04.449
The Darling Home in London is a very sad place.

00:46:04.509 --> 00:46:09.111
Mr. and Mrs. Darling never smile or laugh.

00:46:09.171 --> 00:46:14.168
They always think about Wendy, John and Michael.

00:46:14.228 --> 00:46:20.500
Every morning, at breakfast, Mrs. Darling looks at the three empty chairs and says, 

00:46:20.600 --> 00:46:24.358
Where are my children?

00:46:24.418 --> 00:46:27.190
She has tears in her eyes.

00:46:27.250 --> 00:46:32.733
Nana goes to the nursery and sees three empty beds.

00:46:32.793 --> 00:46:37.200
In the evening, Mr. Darling comes home after work, 

00:46:37.300 --> 00:46:41.773
and he does not hear his children talking and laughing.

00:46:41.833 --> 00:46:48.142
Mrs. Darling often sits in the silent nursery and cries.

00:46:48.202 --> 00:46:54.336
She thinks of her children, their games and their happy voices.

00:46:54.397 --> 00:47:01.071
Nana tries to comfort her, but nothing can make Mrs. Darling happy.

00:47:01.131 --> 00:47:05.454
She always leaves the nursery window open.

00:47:05.514 --> 00:47:10.645
Then one night, something wonderful happens.

00:47:10.705 --> 00:47:16.925
Wendy, John, and Michael fly into the nursery.

00:47:16.985 --> 00:47:21.946
Mrs. Darling is sitting near the fireplace and thinking about her children.

00:47:22.007 --> 00:47:24.818
She hears a voice and turns around.

00:47:24.878 --> 00:47:26.838
Mother, Mother!

00:47:26.898 --> 00:47:28.589
cries Wendy happily.

00:47:28.649 --> 00:47:30.279
We home!

00:47:30.340 --> 00:47:33.870
Mrs. Darling sees Wendy, John, and Michael.

00:47:33.930 --> 00:47:36.051
She is very surprised.

00:47:36.111 --> 00:47:38.300
She cannot believe her eyes.

00:47:38.400 --> 00:47:42.974
She cries.

00:47:43.034 --> 00:47:45.585
Is this true?

00:47:45.645 --> 00:47:50.627
Or is it a dream? Mother!
 
00:47:50.687 --> 00:47:58.070
The children say. It's true! We're home!
 
00:47:58.130 --> 00:48:01.632
They hug their mother and kiss her.

00:48:01.692 --> 00:48:05.323
It's wonderful to see you.

00:48:05.383 --> 00:48:09.200
Says Mrs Darling, looking at her three children.

00:48:09.260 --> 00:48:12.284
Let me look at you.

00:48:12.344 --> 00:48:16.546
How wonderful to hear your sweet voices.

00:48:16.606 --> 00:48:25.300
Nana runs into the nursery and barks happily.

00:48:25.400 --> 00:48:28.979
The children are very pleased to see her.

00:48:29.039 --> 00:48:33.570
I must call your father, says Mrs Darling.

00:48:33.630 --> 00:48:39.012
George, George, come to the nursery immediately.

00:48:39.072 --> 00:48:45.095
Mr. Darling comes to the nursery and sees his three children.

00:48:45.155 --> 00:48:49.008
This is a wonderful night.

00:48:49.068 --> 00:48:50.678
He says happily.

00:48:50.739 --> 00:48:54.730
Our children are finally home.

00:48:54.790 --> 00:48:57.512
Mother. Says Wendy.
 
00:48:57.572 --> 00:49:01.674
Peter Pan and the Lost Boys are here too.

00:49:01.734 --> 00:49:04.536
They're waiting outside.

00:49:04.596 --> 00:49:09.518
Ask them to come inside. Says Mrs. Darling.
 
00:49:09.578 --> 00:49:18.228
The six lost boys slowly enter the nursery and look at Mr. and Mrs. Darling and Nana.

00:49:18.288 --> 00:49:21.050
Mother? says Wendy.
 
00:49:21.110 --> 00:49:23.800
These are the Lost Boys.

00:49:23.860 --> 00:49:27.602
They haven't got a family or a mother.

00:49:27.662 --> 00:49:29.600
Can they stay with us?

00:49:29.700 --> 00:49:40.290
Oh, these dear little boys haven't got a family or a mother. Says Mrs. Darling.
 
00:49:40.350 --> 00:49:43.757
Of course they can stay with us.

00:49:43.817 --> 00:49:46.978
We're their new family.

00:49:47.038 --> 00:49:53.102
Thank you Mrs Darling. Say the Lost Boys.
 
00:49:53.162 --> 00:49:56.344
But where is Peter Pan?

00:49:56.404 --> 00:50:00.638
asks Mrs Darling, looking around the nursery.

00:50:00.698 --> 00:50:09.076
Peter Pan comes into the nursery and says, Here I am, but I don't want to stay here.

00:50:09.136 --> 00:50:13.521
Everyone is surprised, and Mrs Darling asks.

00:50:13.581 --> 00:50:16.812
Why don't you want to stay here?

00:50:16.872 --> 00:50:22.404
I don't want to go to school and learn things. Says Peter.
 
00:50:22.464 --> 00:50:24.625
I don't want to grow up.

00:50:24.685 --> 00:50:29.936
I want to be a young boy and have lots of fun forever.

00:50:29.996 --> 00:50:34.048
But Peter. Says Wendy sadly.
 
00:50:34.108 --> 00:50:38.018
I must go back to Neverland. Says Peter.
 
00:50:38.078 --> 00:50:41.740
my home and my friends are there.

00:50:41.800 --> 00:50:46.202
I'm happy with the Indians and the fairies.

00:50:46.262 --> 00:50:52.886
Wendy is surprised and asks, when can I see you then?

00:50:52.946 --> 00:50:59.916
Mrs Darling thinks for a moment and says, I have a good idea.

00:50:59.976 --> 00:51:05.780
Wendy, you can visit Peter in Neverland every spring.

00:51:05.840 --> 00:51:09.222
You can stay there for a week.

00:51:09.283 --> 00:51:15.428
Can I really go to Neverland every spring, Mother? asks Wendy.
 
00:51:15.488 --> 00:51:18.220
Of course you can.

00:51:18.280 --> 00:51:21.502
Says Mrs Darling smiling.

00:51:21.562 --> 00:51:26.840
Peter looks at Mrs Darling and asks, Is that a promise?

00:51:26.900 --> 00:51:28.761
Of course it is.

00:51:28.821 --> 00:51:30.561
Says Mrs Darling.

00:51:30.621 --> 00:51:35.700
Then I want Spring to come quickly. Says Peter happily.
 
00:51:35.800 --> 00:51:41.814
Yes, very quickly. Says Wendy laughing.
 
00:51:41.874 --> 00:51:44.764
Come on Tink. Says Peter.
 
00:51:44.824 --> 00:51:48.778
Let's fly home and wait for Spring.

00:51:48.839 --> 00:51:56.268
Peter Pan and Tinker Bell fly out of the nursery window and into the night sky.

00:51:56.328 --> 00:52:01.272
They are flying to Neverland.

00:52:01.332 --> 00:52:04.333
Exercise three.

00:52:04.394 --> 00:52:09.208
Wendy is taking the Lost Boys on a short tour of London.

00:52:09.268 --> 00:52:12.640
She is giving them some information about the city.

00:52:12.700 --> 00:52:17.268
Listen to her and then choose the correct answer.

00:52:17.328 --> 00:52:23.783
Today we're going to visit some interesting places in London.

00:52:23.843 --> 00:52:32.384
The first place we're going to see is Big Ben, the big clock tower near the houses of Parliament.

00:52:32.444 --> 00:52:36.395
Look at the clock at the top of the tower.

00:52:36.455 --> 00:52:40.396
Now we're going to travel on the River Thames.

00:52:40.456 --> 00:52:42.716
Let's buy tickets.

00:52:42.776 --> 00:52:46.654
It's always fun to ride a boat on the river.

00:52:46.714 --> 00:52:50.123
We're going to see Tower Bridge.

00:52:50.184 --> 00:52:56.257
The bridge sometimes opens up to let big ships pass.

00:52:56.318 --> 00:53:00.870
The Tower of London is near Tower Bridge.

00:53:00.930 --> 00:53:05.454
It's very old and a lot of people visit it.

00:53:05.514 --> 00:53:09.506
Let's walk by this beautiful church.

00:53:09.567 --> 00:53:11.878
It's St Paul's Cathedral.

00:53:11.938 --> 00:53:15.652
The people of London love this church.

00:53:15.712 --> 00:53:20.635
Oh, it's a quarter past one and time for lunch.

00:53:20.695 --> 00:53:24.286
After lunch, we're going to Hyde Park.

00:53:24.346 --> 00:53:27.087
It's a wonderful big park.

00:53:27.147 --> 00:53:30.918
We can play there until half past four.

00:53:30.978 --> 00:53:34.900
Then we must go home for tea.

00:53:34.960 --> 00:53:42.311
The Darling Home What does the Darling Home in London look like?

00:53:42.371 --> 00:53:46.210
It is a comfortable home with a nice garden.

00:53:46.270 --> 00:53:49.838
On the ground floor, there is a dining room.

00:53:49.899 --> 00:53:52.729
The family has its meals here.

00:53:52.789 --> 00:53:57.010
There is a long table with a lot of chairs around it.

00:53:57.070 --> 00:54:00.490
There are also pictures on the walls.

00:54:00.550 --> 00:54:08.582
On the ground floor, there is also a large sitting room with a big sofa and comfortable chairs.

00:54:08.642 --> 00:54:13.232
People sit here in the evening and read or talk.

00:54:13.292 --> 00:54:16.219
They also listen to music.

00:54:16.279 --> 00:54:19.476
Families like singing together.

00:54:19.536 --> 00:54:22.176
Often someone plays the piano.

00:54:22.236 --> 00:54:26.558
When friends come to visit, they sit in the sitting room.

00:54:26.618 --> 00:54:30.889
At the back of the house, there is a big kitchen.

00:54:30.949 --> 00:54:36.660
Next to the kitchen, there is a small room called the scullery.

00:54:36.720 --> 00:54:40.212
This is where the servants wash up.

00:54:40.272 --> 00:54:45.857
Some big houses have breakfast rooms and libraries.

00:54:45.917 --> 00:54:52.179
On the first floor, there are the bedrooms, the bathroom and the nursery.

00:54:52.239 --> 00:54:55.794
The rooms have open fireplaces.

00:54:55.854 --> 00:55:00.010
The servants live in rooms at the top of the house.